1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,758
The suitcase was purple, just like the
message said. The clown inside

2
00:00:04,758 --> 00:00:06,740
wasn't part of their deal.

3
00:00:06,740 --> 00:00:11,500
Lucia lifted a sequined jacket. Jason
found giant shoes, stage makeup, and

4
00:00:11,500 --> 00:00:13,880
a drawing embroidered into the lining.

5
00:00:13,880 --> 00:00:19,029
They had taken the wrong case from a
crowded depot, certain every purple

6
00:00:19,029 --> 00:00:21,010
suitcase belonged to their contact.

7
00:00:21,010 --> 00:00:24,578
A public announcement asked for missing
theatre costumes. Tomorrow's

8
00:00:24,578 --> 00:00:27,750
children's performance had already sold
every seat available.

9
00:00:27,750 --> 00:00:32,111
Jason checked the clock. Their real
pickup window was closing. Lucia

10
00:00:32,111 --> 00:00:34,490
zipped the costume case shut anyway.

11
00:00:34,490 --> 00:00:39,243
They carried it to lost property, where
a performer pressed both hands

12
00:00:39,243 --> 00:00:41,620
against the purple lid in relief.

13
00:00:41,620 --> 00:00:45,981
Their contact stopped answering. No
case, no payment. Jason sat beside

14
00:00:45,981 --> 00:00:48,360
Lucia beneath the departures board,
silent.

15
00:00:48,360 --> 00:00:53,878
Then he found one silver sequin on his
sleeve. She grinned. First honest

16
00:00:53,878 --> 00:00:56,000
tip we'd earned all week.
